<newsitem itemid="79530" id="root" date="1996-09-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Norcor H1 pretax profit slips.</title>
<headline>Norcor H1 pretax profit slips.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		0.9		    vs 5.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.1		    vs 1.65</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.35		   vs 1.98</p>
<p> Turnover		   24.87		  vs 28.76</p>
<p> Operating result	 0.61		   vs 2.08</p>
<p> Interest		   0.27		   vs 0.10</p>
<p> Tax			  0.12		   vs 0.56</p>
<p> Attributable	loss 0.06		   vs 0.98 profit</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 22</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 15</p>
<p> Ex-div date		October 7</p>
<p>Note - Corrugated board maker Norcor Holdings Plc said it did not expect a significant change in the trading environment &quot;within the immediate future.&quot; It said a strategic review had identified areas for cost savings and the benefits from these would &quot;increasingly come through over the next twelve months.&quot; But it added that initially, these would be offset in part by related and necessary one-off costs.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
